{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And lovingkindness</b> — this is the reward of the righteous, which is forever. And it is stated in the Torah for His lovers — they being at the highest rank — and afterward, <b>to those who keep His commandments</b> — out of fear. And thus its interpretation here: <b>to those who fear Him</b>, and they are the keepers of His covenant; <b>only those who remember His precepts</b> — they are the lovers, for His precepts are always before them, and in their heart they will not be forgotten for a single moment."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 103, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:03.145740011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}